\begin_layout Subsection
Standard Delay Format Simulations
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
SDF (Standard Delay Format) simulations are a specialized form of gate-level
 simulation where precise timing delays are back-annotated into the netlist
 using an .sdf file generated after synthesis or place-and-route.
 These delays represent real-world propagation times through gates and interconn
ects, capturing setup and hold checks, clock skew, and data path delays.
 SDF simulations are essential for verifying the timing behavior of a design
 under realistic conditions, ensuring that it meets all timing constraints
 such as clock-to-Q, combinational path delays, and input/output timing.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The testbench design may change as we move from functional simulation to
 SDF simulations, hence `define or `ifdef SDF kind of macros could be used
 if we selectively want a part of testbench to be active during that testing.
 
\end_layout

